Abstract = {Standardized analysis pipelines contribute to making data bioinformatics
   research compliant with the paradigm of Findability, Accessibility,
   Interoperability, and Reusability (FAIR), and facilitate collaboration.
   Nextflow and Snakemake, two popular command-line solutions, are
   increasingly adopted by users, complementing GUI-based platforms such as
   Galaxy. We report recent developments of the nf-core framework with the
   new Nextflow Domain-Specific Language (DSL2). An extensive library of
   modules and subworkflows enables research communities to adopt common
   standards progressively, as resources and needs allow. We present an
   overview of some of the research communities built around nf-core and
   showcase its adoption by six EuroFAANG farmed animal research consortia.},
